<newsitem itemid="73402" id="root" date="1996-09-24" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Exceptionals push Ruberoid into H1 loss.</title>
<headline>Exceptionals push Ruberoid into H1 loss.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)(adjusted)  0.2		    vs 3.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.9		    vs 1.9</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.96 loss	    vs 2.69 profit</p>
<p> Turnover		   102.62		 vs 99.49</p>
<p> Operating result	 1.13		   vs 3.43</p>
<p> Exceptional		1.14 loss	    vs nil</p>
<p> Interest		   0.94		   vs 0.74</p>
<p> Tax			  0.07		   vs 0.95</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1.03 loss	    vs 1.74 profit</p>
<p> Retained		   1.95 loss	    vs 0.82 profit</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 22</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 22</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 14</p>
<p>Note - Ruberoid, a specialist waterproofing systems and protective coatings maker, said it intended to maintain its total dividend at 6.1 pence per share barring unforeseen circumstances.</p>
<p>Chairman David Kendall said contracting order books &quot;are very satisfactory,&quot; but added that he was disappointed with the results.</p>
<p>But he added that market positions are secure, product quality and service levels excellent and action is being taken to improve the quality of earnings, all of which should show benefits in 1997.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
